The `findymail` MCP server exposes 14 tools. Every lookup tool works on ONE record per call: there is no batch endpoint, so a list of 200 people is 200 calls. Loop, keep going when a single call fails, and write partial results as you go.

## Pick the tool

| Need | Tool | Input | Cost |
|------|------|-------|------|
| Email for one person | `find_email` | `name` + `domain`, or `linkedin_url` (URL wins if both) | 1 finder credit if found, free otherwise |
| People holding given titles at a company | `find_employees` | `website`, `job_titles` (max 10), `count` (1 to 5) | 1 finder credit per contact returned |
| Phone number | `find_phone` | `linkedin_url` only | 10 finder credits if found, free otherwise |
| Is this address deliverable | `verify_email` | `email` | 1 verifier credit (separate pool) |
| Who owns this address | `reverse_email_lookup` | `email`, `with_profile` | 1 credit for the LinkedIn URL, 2 with full profile, free if nobody matches |
| Firmographics for one company | `enrich_company` | `domain`, `linkedin_url`, or `name` (domain wins) | 1 finder credit if found |
| Companies matching a description | `generate_lead_list` then `get_lead_list_results` | plain-language `query`, `mode`, enrichment flags | see below |
| Companies similar to a seed | `lookalike_search` | `seed` domain, `same_country`, `same_size`, `limit` | 1 finder credit per 10 results |
| Manage excluded domains | `list_exclusion_lists`, `create_exclusion_list`, `list_exclusion_domains`, `add_exclusion_domains`, `remove_exclusion_domains` | see tool schemas | free |

`generate_lead_list` cost: 1 credit per 10 companies in `broad` mode or 1 credit per company in `targeted` mode, plus 1 per contact found, 1 per email found, and 10 per phone found. `get_lead_list_results` is free.

## How the tools chain

- Company list -> people: `generate_lead_list` or `lookalike_search` -> `find_employees` (or let `generate_lead_list` fetch contacts itself with `find_contact: true`).
- Person -> email: `find_employees` returns name, title and LinkedIn URL but no email. Pass the LinkedIn URL (preferred) or name + domain to `find_email`.
- Anything -> phone: `find_phone` needs a LinkedIn URL. Get it from `find_employees`, `reverse_email_lookup`, or the user. A phone cannot be found from a name or an email alone.
- Unknown email -> person: `reverse_email_lookup`. It says nothing about deliverability; use `verify_email` for that.
- Company name only -> domain: `enrich_company` by name, or ask the user when the name is ambiguous.

## Guardrails

- Emails from `find_email` and `generate_lead_list` are already verified. Do not run `verify_email` on them.
- Never guess or construct an email address. A not-found result is the answer; report it as not found.
- Before a run that can spend more than 25 credits (a list of 25+ people, a lead list with contacts, any phone lookups), state the maximum cost and get the user's go-ahead.
- Phone lookups are 10 credits each. Only call `find_phone` when the user explicitly asked for phone numbers.
- For a lead list, start with a small validation run (`limit` 10 to 20, `find_contact: false`), review the companies, refine the query, then scale up. Never start a second `generate_lead_list` for the same query while the first is still processing: each run is billed.
- `exclusion_list_ids` on `generate_lead_list`: pass exactly `[0]` (every exclusion source you can reach), exactly `[-1]` (no filtering), or real list ids. Never mix markers with ids. `lookalike_search` accepts real ids only.
- `remove_exclusion_domains` is permanent and takes domain ids, not names. Call `list_exclusion_domains` with an explicit `list_id` first, show the user what will be removed, and confirm.
- `add_exclusion_domains` applies the first 50 domains immediately and queues the rest; read the list back before relying on it.
- Error handling: 402 means the account is out of credits, stop and point the user to https://app.findymail.com to top up. 429 means rate limited, wait and retry. 401 means the sign-in expired, ask the user to reconnect the Findymail MCP server in Cursor settings.
- Free-mail domains (gmail.com, outlook.com, yahoo.com) are not company domains. `find_email` needs the employer's domain.
